==German==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|de|gmh|tunkel}}, from {{inh|de|goh|tunkal}}, {{m|goh|tuncal||dark}}, from {{inh|de|gem-pro|*dunkalaz||dark}}, from {{inh|de|ine-pro|*dʰengw-||to smoke, fume}}. The modern consonantism is [[Central German|Central]] and [[Low German]] (compare {{etyl|gml|de}} {{m|gml|dunker}}, also {{m|gml|dunkel}}). Cognate to {{cog|nl|donker||dark}}.

===Pronunciation===
